url: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/symmetric-hadamard-4356"
license: GPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  A short note updating two entries of the 2025 Đoković–Seberry census of
  symmetric Hadamard matrices of order 4v, v odd: v = 529 and v = 1089 are
  listed as undecided. No new construction is involved. Wallis and Whiteman (1972) give
  a regular symmetric Hadamard matrix with constant diagonal of order (p-1)^2
  from a symmetric conference matrix of order p-1, p a prime power; Gritsenko
  (2021) supplies a symmetric conference matrix of order 66, and Mathon (1978)
  one of order 46. With p = 67 and p = 47 this gives orders 4356 = 4·1089 and
  2116 = 4·529. SageMath already implements the construction and recognizes
  both orders. The repository builds the matrix of order 4356 and checks it
  exactly. Novelty is bounded to the sources searched.
keywords:
  - Hadamard matrices
  - symmetric Hadamard matrices
  - conference matrices
  - strongly regular graphs
